<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks rise.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks rise.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			17/4/97		  10/4/97	     19/4/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	600-625			575		   475</p>
<p>    Naphtha	  75-100		    50-75		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil   1,650-1,700	    1,700-1,750		 1,600</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	350-375			325		   325</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     10			 10		    10</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks rose despite swift throughput of product.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks were up as product arriving by cargo outweighed departures to the mogas pool and the chemical sector.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks fell despite the arrival of cargoes from Russia. Some product left for the traditional barge markets. Other product departed in cargoes to the Asia Pacific region.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks rose as Russian straight-run arrived. Barges and bunkers departed and some vacuum gas oil headed down the Rhine.</p>
<p>Jet fuel stocks barely changed.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
